    rdf:value """he has never liked Obrist or Blaydes or Andersen – all people to whom he has been most awfully kind and sympathetic. The people he instinctively  likes , in that nice intimate,  sour-give  way, are Trevy and Fafner (who is going to be married to a journalist, Miss Boyce), Carpenter, Reinach, Zangwill, Placci. Finished Fra Bartolommeo.
Friday, May 19.99. Frullino Florence.
Doctor and music and a quiet day. The Venetian furniture arrived. Count Stroganoff and the Marchesa Incontri had tea with Bernhard, and afterwards he went for a walk and called on Mr. Ross. He finished Robertson’s  History of Free Thought . 
X  X  X  X
X  X  X
X  X
Saturday May 20. 1899.
The Houghtons called. Miss Erichsen came to lunch. Bernhard lunched """^^xsd:string ;
